Went through all 8 units, judging each candidate against the semantic-linefeeds rule (fused → split at sentence ends only; wrap → rejoin then re-split only at real clause boundaries — `;`, `:`, `—`, and/but/so joining two independent clauses, or a subordinator/relative pronoun opening a clause — and only when the resulting line still exceeds ~120 chars). Unit 3 has no candidate that achieves full one-sentence-per-line without leaving multiple sentences fused together, so I've supplied a `missing` repair for it.

