A few notes on the judgment calls:

- **Unit 3**: every candidate leaves at least two full sentences fused on one line (mostly sentences 2/3, or 2/3/4). None reaches one-sentence-per-line, so I rejected all and supplied the full repair. Sentence 1 and the tail of sentence 4 have no recognized clause boundary at all (confirmed by the checker's own `long`-with-no-boundary advisory quoting sentence 1) and stay long by design.
- **Units 5–6**: candidates that split inside `` `//go:packed` `` mid-token, or split a short (<120-char) sentence at an unneeded comma/em-dash, were rejected — the rule only re-splits at sentence ends unless the line is still over length.
- **Unit 8**: only c05 both fixes the fused `repo. Of course...` boundary and picks the one real boundary (`released, and then...`, a coordinating conjunction joining two independent clauses) needed because the rejoined sentence exceeds 120 chars; all others either leave `repo.`/`Of course,` fused or split at a non-boundary comma (`course,`, `modules,`).
